<section id="image-text-policy" class="image-text-policy" aria-labelledby="image-text-policy-title">
  <label id="image-text-policy-title" class="image-text-toggle" for="image-text-enabled"><input id="image-text-enabled" type="checkbox">Text in the image</label>
  <p class="image-help">Without this option, the render is told to draw no text. The entered brief is kept.</p>
  <div id="image-text-options" hidden>
    <label for="image-text-strategy">How should the text be prepared?</label>
    <select id="image-text-strategy"><option value="auto">Hermes advises</option><option value="single-pass">One pass · text generated with the image</option><option value="two-pass">Two passes · image, then exact layers</option></select>
    <p class="image-help">Hermes helps choose the essential text and its placement. A few words can be tried in the render; many or precise names can be added afterwards as layers.</p>
    <ol id="image-text-policy-labels" class="image-text-policy-labels"></ol>
    <div class="image-text-policy-actions"><button id="image-text-policy-add" type="button" class="quiet-button">Add an exact text</button><button id="image-text-policy-advice" type="button" class="quiet-button">Prepare the text with Hermes</button></div>
  </div>
  <p id="image-text-policy-status" class="image-help" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
</section>
